     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "{\"unit_id\": \"Meryetamun\", \"choices\": [\"C2\"], \"reasoning\": \"C1 Mr.t-Mnw is 'Meret-Min', the words mr.t 'beloved' plus the god's name Min (Mnw). Record 1 ends in 'amun', which renders the god Amun, not Min. Its consonants do not fit either: the w of Mnw follows n, but 'amun' has its u before the n. So C1 is a different name. C2 Mr.t-Jmn is 'Meret-Imen', the words mr.t 'beloved' plus Jmn (Amun). Record 1 reads as Mery(e)t = m-r-t with conventional vowels, then amun = Jmn, with j rendered as a, m, an added u, and n. That is exactly those words in the same order, so C2 is the same name.\"}"
     }
